{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788384457859,"sessionID":"ses_f9bfb8556ffen7Iyy24hTmtXJA","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-89644719c5b487b0","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"gh issue view 149 --repo kantord/toylang; echo \"exit: $?\""},"output":"title:\tImplement Float (IEEE binary64 per ADR 0007) across the backends\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tkantord (Dániel Kántor)\nlabels:\t\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\t\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t149\n--\nBuild the Float type end to end, per docs/adr/0007-float-is-javascripts-double.md: IEEE 754\nbinary64, matching JavaScript's number representation, no alternative width, no decimal type.\n\nSemantics per gh:145 (the Q37 ruling): admit NaN/Infinity, division by zero returns Infinity\n(IEEE), matching IEEE 754. Division is a total function on Float; Int and Float division have\ndifferent failure behavior (Int still raises on zero divisor).\n\nNot yet settled, needs a call during implementation: exact float literal printing so all seven\nbackends agree byte for byte (default float formatting differs across languages) -- pick a\nformat and hold every backend to it. See draft.md Q37 in plans/questions.md for the fuller\nquestion shape if it still exists, otherwise use the ADR and gh:145 as the source of truth.\n\nAcceptance:\n- Float literals parse and type-check\n- arithmetic (+ - * /) and comparisons work across all seven backends with agreeing output\n- NaN/Infinity are producible and print identically across backends\n- division by zero on Float returns Infinity, not an error (contrast with Int)\n- corpus test coverage added for the above\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nexit: 0\n","metadata":{"output":"title:\tImplement Float (IEEE binary64 per ADR 0007) across the backends\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tkantord (Dániel Kántor)\nlabels:\t\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\t\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t149\n--\nBuild the Float type end to end, per docs/adr/0007-float-is-javascripts-double.md: IEEE 754\nbinary64, matching JavaScript's number representation, no alternative width, no decimal type.\n\nSemantics per gh:145 (the Q37 ruling): admit NaN/Infinity, division by zero returns Infinity\n(IEEE), matching IEEE 754. Division is a total function on Float; Int and Float division have\ndifferent failure behavior (Int still raises on zero divisor).\n\nNot yet settled, needs a call during implementation: exact float literal printing so all seven\nbackends agree byte for byte (default float formatting differs across languages) -- pick a\nformat and hold every backend to it. See draft.md Q37 in plans/questions.md for the fuller\nquestion shape if it still exists, otherwise use the ADR and gh:145 as the source of truth.\n\nAcceptance:\n- Float literals parse and type-check\n- arithmetic (+ - * /) and comparisons work across all seven backends with agreeing output\n- NaN/Infinity are producible and print identically across backends\n- division by zero on Float returns Infinity, not an error (contrast with Int)\n- corpus test coverage added for the above\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nexit: 0\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"gh issue view 149 --repo kantord/toylang; echo \"exit: $?\"","time":{"start":1788384457855,"end":1788384457857}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Empty output. Let me try without --comments and check the exit status.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_06405302d001y6LsDLz8243ZGK","sessionID":"ses_f9bfb8556ffen7Iyy24hTmtXJA","messageID":"msg_064052623001VeQycAAYBYLZz6"}}
