{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788384539452,"sessionID":"ses_f9bfb8556ffen7Iyy24hTmtXJA","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_f6357e8a3ae64081bd4438ec","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n -B2 -A8 \"float-format-research|float-build-lua|status: delegated|float-format\" plans/board.yaml | head -80"},"output":"1-- id: stuck-issue-168-investigation\n2-  kind: build\n3:  status: delegated\n4-  needs: []\n5-  issue: gh:168\n6-  title: 'INVESTIGATE stuck lane issue-168 (no activity 4h, 2 run(s), 0 commits): evidence frozen in plans/incidents/issue-168-20260902/ -- read it plus the lane worktree, then report in plans/opencode-rollout.md whether this was brief clarity, a capability gap, a tooling/permission trap, or task shape, and propose the rebrief or reshape. Do NOT attempt the original task.'\n7-- id: stuck-issue-153-investigation\n8-  kind: build\n9:  status: delegated\n10-  needs: []\n11-  issue: gh:153\n12-  title: 'INVESTIGATE stuck lane issue-153 (no activity 2h, 2 run(s), 0 commits): evidence frozen in plans/incidents/issue-153-20260902/ -- read it plus the lane worktree, then report in plans/opencode-rollout.md whether this was brief clarity, a capability gap, a tooling/permission trap, or task shape, and propose the rebrief or reshape. Do NOT attempt the original task.'\n13-- id: function-signature-matching-syntax\n14-  issue: gh:152\n15-  title: 'Grill the concrete spelling for implicit-. params via matching syntax -- round 1 couldn''t pick without more context; round 2 presents the maintainer''s own hoist-into-signature sketch (fn render = Msg(Ping -> ... or ...)) as a concrete candidate (gh:152). Round 2 answer: no pick yet; round 3 stress-tested each of the three candidates (A/B/C) against the real parser and re-asked. Round 3 answer: still no pick, needs signature-matching-deeper-research first; round 4 presented that research (all six type shapes) with full code probes per option. Round 4 answer: still no pick, and it is process feedback, not a content signal -- option cards were too long (\"at least 8 times shorter\"), code belongs once in the thesis not repeated per option, and rounds should frame how each option interacts with future plans rather than asking for an early commit. grill-via-annotations/SKILL.md''s option-card rule updated to match (2026-09-02). Round 5 must re-ask the same A/B/C content (A and B still fail identically pre-shape, C still the only candidate that parses all six shapes) in the new short-card, future-framed shape -- no new research needed.'\n16-  kind: decide\n17-  needs: [signature-matching-deeper-research]\n--\n25-  needs: []\n26-  prio: 3\n27:  status: delegated\n28-\n29-- id: dsv-partials-migration\n30-  issue: gh:136\n31-  title: 'Ruled provisional (prelude-partials-and-mutation round): csv/tsv stay compiler-predefined names until source_in_fn allows stream sources inside function bodies AND a partial-application mechanism is ratified+built -- then move both into prelude.toy as ordinary shadowable partials. Blocked-open, not a live task yet.'\n32-  kind: build\n33-  needs: [partial-application-system-design]\n34-  prio: 5\n35-  status: todo\n--\n71-  needs: []\n72-  prio: 1\n73:  status: delegated\n74-\n75-- id: stdin-redesign-build-2\n76-  issue: gh:172\n77-  title: 'Re-file of gh:159 (maintainer cleanup ruling, 2026-09-02, option C: drop the poisoned issue-159 lane, re-board under a fresh lane id rather than repair it). Retire the three stdin keywords for one Stream<Str> source, parse(.) as a library call (stdin-syntax-design ruling, tentative -- verify parse(.) resolves an expected type inside a map body before full build). The old issue-159 branch/worktree are abandoned in place (permission-denied cleanup, left as garbage per the ruling); the feature diff there (commit 45c76be) is reference-only, re-derive against current main rather than cherry-pick.'\n78-  kind: build\n79-  needs: []\n80-  model: fable\n81:  status: delegated\n82-\n83-- id: trait-interface-build\n84-  issue: gh:174\n85-  title: 'Ruled (trait-interface-design round): (1) Rust-shaped declaration -- trait Name { fn sig(...) -> T } / impl Name for Type { fn sig(...) -> T = body }; (2) builtin operators (Int+Int, Str+Str, ...) tentatively become source-written prelude impls \"when practical, otherwise built in\" -- maintainer explicitly declined to fully commit either way (\"in some cases performance may decide this... we would need to see how it works out in practice\"), so start with prelude impls (uniform, matches the mechanism) and fall back to checker-generated only where the prelude indirection provably costs real performance; revisit once build experience exists; (3) named trait methods are colon-only -- x:foo(y) is the only spelling, no plain-call fallback even when unambiguous.'\n86-  kind: build\n87-  needs: []\n88:  status: delegated\n89-\n90-- id: mutation-semantics-spike\n91-  title: 'Ruled (prelude-partials-and-mutation round): maintainer leans privileged/shared-reference mutation-as-optimization but will not ratify without prototyping -- spike the \"provably one reference exists\" static analysis against a couple of backends before a real decide row reopens this'\n92-  kind: build\n93-  needs: []\n94-  prio: 4\n95-  status: todo\n96-\n--\n100-  kind: build\n101-  needs: [float-build]\n102:  status: delegated\n103-\n104-- id: float-build-python\n105-  issue: gh:149\n106-  title: Implement Float (IEEE binary64 per ADR 0007) for the Python backend only, following float-build's JS implementation as the reference. One backend, one commit.\n107-  kind: build\n108-  needs: [float-build]\n109:  status: delegated\n110-\n111-- id: float-build-go\n112-  issue: gh:149\n113-  title: Implement Float (IEEE binary64 per ADR 0007) for the Go backend only, following float-build's JS implementation as the reference. One backend, one commit.\n114-  kind: build\n115-  needs: [float-build]\n116:  status: delegated\n117-\n118:- id: float-build-lua\n